Mark the eMMC factory partition node as a GPT partition so the block NVMEM
provider can expose the LAN/WAN MAC cells referenced by qcom-ppe.

Without this compatible, qcom-ppe remains in deferred probe and no wired
Ethernet ports are registered.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts
@@ -183,6 +183,8 @@
 			compatible = "block-device";
 
 			partitions {
+				compatible = "gpt-partitions";
+
 				block-partition-factory {
 					partname = "factory";
 
